# Security headers for intersecting-parallels.pages.dev — Doctrine §16.6
#
# The CSP was widened DELIBERATELY when the app replaced the placeholder, which
# is what the placeholder's own note asked the next session to do rather than
# discover through a broken deploy.
#
# What changed and why:
#   script-src 'self'   — the app is ES modules under /app/. There is NO inline
#                         script anywhere in index.html, so 'unsafe-inline' is
#                         not needed and is not granted: a strict script-src is
#                         the single most valuable directive here and it costs
#                         nothing because the code was written to files from
#                         the start.
#   style-src  'self' 'unsafe-inline'
#                       — the stylesheet is /app.css, but the renderer positions
#                         off-canvas vanishing-point markers by setting
#                         element.style, and Safari applies CSP to that path.
#                         Stated plainly rather than implied: this is the one
#                         concession, and it is styling only.
#   img-src 'self' data: blob:
#                       — blob: is the PNG export previewing and downloading its
#                         own output; data: is the inline favicon.
#   connect-src 'self'  — the app never calls out. Nothing to fetch at runtime
#                         (§7), so anything trying to is a bug or an intrusion.
#   worker-src 'self'   — the service worker that makes it work offline.
#
# No Strict-Transport-Security: pages.dev is HTTPS-only and Cloudflare handles
# TLS; a lock-in header that cannot be tested from here would be worse than
# leaving it to the platform.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# The service worker must never be served stale, or an update can be pinned to
# a cached copy of the old one.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
